        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "Inputs for `cerner_updateCondition` (FHIR R4 PUT `/Condition/{id}`).\n\nCerner requires `If-Match: W/\"<versionId>\"` (pass via `options.ifMatch`) for optimistic concurrency — fetch the Condition first (`cerner_getCondition`) and read `meta.versionId`. `code`, `category`, and `note` are IMMUTABLE on update — Cerner returns 200 but silently discards changes to them; send the existing values verbatim. To change a Condition's lifecycle, set `clinicalStatus`/`verificationStatus` (this is how you reach `refuted` / `entered-in-error`, which create cannot set).",
